<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Viducasses</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.) · capital Aregenua</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Small Gallic people of the Caen plain whose Roman town at Vieux has yielded the famous Thorigny marble.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Known from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pliny-the-elder">Pliny</a> and Ptolemy, the Viducasses lived south of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caen">Caen</a> in lower <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-normandy">Normandy</a>. They were probably included among the Armorican peoples in Caesar's time.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is recorded of their rulers. Their chief town, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aregenua">Aregenua</a>, lay at Vieux.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aregenua">Aregenua</a> became a prosperous civitas capital with baths and fine houses. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thorigny-marble">Thorigny marble</a>, an inscription of 238 CE, honours one of its citizens, Titus Sennius Sollemnis. The civitas later merged with that of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/baiocasses">Baiocasses</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:53.73%;width:4.86%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Aregenua</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=viducasses" aria-label="Viducasses on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4706 533 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Viducasses lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5026 789h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5026 789h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=viducasses">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

